I built the issue desk in `src/` as XState v5 machines: a desk root that owns the three pages and the open-issue count, plus an issues machine, a help machine and a settings machine. Each server write runs as its own spawned promise actor with its own rollback, so overlapping writes settle independently. `./check` passes and all 30 visible tests pass (6 of the 15 runs used). I also probed the decline and rollback paths with mocked backends outside the browser, and they behave as the brief describes.

Things I was unsure about: a declined assignment shows `assign error: declined` in the detail, since the brief gives only the server's message. Titles, labels and comments are trimmed before they are sent, and adding a label is ignored until the label list has loaded. The browser run printed one 404 console error that I could not trace to the app's own requests.